SUMMARY: Singles | Soundtracks of a Generation
DESCRIPTION:Arranged as an episodic comedy\, Singles spotlights the inter
 twined lives of the co-habitants\, friends\, and bandmates of the same Se
 attle apartment building. Foregrounded by the tumultuous romantic relatio
 nship between Steve (Campbell Scott) and Linda (Kyra Sedgwick)—who meet a
 t an Alice in Chains concert\, of course!—the drama extends to their frie
 ndship with Janet Livermore (Bridget Fonda)\, who is tirelessly trying to
  win the affection of grunge-rocker Cliff Poncier (Matt Dillon). as well 
 as their neighbor Debbie Hunt (Sheila Kelly)\, who is aching for a husban
 d who appreciates her and her fantastic earrings. The film also features 
 an endless stream of stellar cameos\, including Eric Stoltz\, Bill Pullma
 n\, Tom Skerritt\, Peter Horton\, Tim Burton\, Eddie Vedder\, and so many
  more! And\, of course\, the soundtrack is a who's who of grunge gods: Pe
 arl Jam\, Mother Love Bone\, Soundgarden\, Alice in Chains\, and Mudhoney
 \, rounded out with the likes of The Smashing Pumpkins\, The Screaming Tr
 ees\, and Paul Westerberg. [99 min\; comedy\, drama\, romance\; English]
CATEGORIES:
