SUMMARY: Thursday Music Night W/ dwBrykalski (a.k.a. David Wierhake) “Mis
 souri Mad-Mule Roots Music” with special guest\, Sarah Flint
DESCRIPTION:Opening (6pm): Sarah Flint is a songwriter\, musician and mus
 ic teacher performing in Bloomington and Brown County\, IN. She performs 
 solo\, and as duo (with Christy Crandell)\, and in Arom Heart Mother\, a 
 Pink Floyd tribute band. Sarah provided backing vocals on John Mellencamp
 's R.O.C.K in the USA from the album Scarecrow (1985). She also offers gu
 itar\, flute and ukulele lessons.\n\nSarah will open our evening at 6pm a
 s a solo artist\, sharing songs by Joni Mitchell.\n\nFollowed by: David W
 ierhake (a.k.a. dwBrykalski)\n\nFrom musical collaborations with John Mel
 lencamp to Craig Brenner to Carrie Newcomer to Tim Grimm to a variety of 
 Bloomington and beyond musicians\, David Wierhake (a.k.a. dwBrykalski) ha
 s gleaned a wealth of creative energy and parleyed it into his own songwr
 iting adventures. A native of the great state of Missouri\, he refers to 
 his musical genre as “Missouri Mad-Mule Roots Music”.\n\nDavid is excited
  about and blessed by Jaime’s invitation to share his songs of “Life\, Lo
 ve\, and Death.” with Juniper Art Gallery’s audience of friends\, neighbo
 rs\, and strangers. His creative energy will be channeled through his gui
 tar\, harmonica\, accordion\, piano\, and his Tom Waits/Leonard Coen-styl
 e voice.\n\nCome early for a drink or snack\; shop for gifts and art. As 
 always\, everyone is welcome!\n\n
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Music
