SUMMARY: Art Colony Weekend 2026 !
DESCRIPTION:Brown County Art Colony Weekend 2026\n\nCalling all art enthu
 siasts to join in on the fun! Art Colony Weekend is a perfect opportunity
  to experience the fall splendor of Brown County. Learn more about the Mi
 dwest Art Colony artists\, enjoy live music while viewing a beautifully c
 urated historic collection\, and attend an auction filled with award-winn
 ing art to purchase. There are a variety of events over three days from w
 hich to choose from.\n\nFriday / September 11\n\nGallery Hop\n\n5 – 7 pm\
 n\nTown of Nashville\n\nFree and open to the public\n\nBegin the weekend 
 celebration by touring participating galleries in the village of Nashvill
 e. The Art Guild will showcase a new Founders Exhibition along with strik
 ing artwork by its current artist members. Live painting by Art Guild Mem
 bers in the Guild galleries\, music & refreshments. The Brown County Craf
 t Guild\, Hoosier Artist Gallery & Spears Gallery will also offer unique 
 and exquisite items for sale.\n\n\nA Founders Exhibition - Frederick W. R
 igley\n\nExhibition Opening\n\n11 am – 7 pm\n\nBrown County Art Guild\n\n
 Free and open to the public\n\nThe Brown County Art Guild proudly present
 s the Founders Exhibition: Frederick W. Rigley\, honoring one of the Guil
 d’s founding artists and an important figure in the development of Brown 
 County’s artistic legacy. Drawn from private collections\, this exhibitio
 n brings together a rare selection of paintings that reflect Rigley’s dee
 p appreciation for the landscapes\, light\, and character of southern Ind
 iana.\n\n\nSaturday / September 12\n\nGreat Outdoor Art Contest\n\n7 am –
  4 pm\n\nT.C. Steele State Historic Site\n\nAdmission fee\n\nThe oldest p
 lein air painting competition in Indiana celebrates its 38th year! Gates 
 open at 7 am for artists to have their canvases stamped and then off to w
 ork. The artwork will be judged at 2 pm with award announcements beginnin
 g at 3:30 pm. A separate admission fee applies for those observing throug
 hout the day or attending the awards ceremony. Details can be found at:\n
 \nhttps://www.indianamuseum.org/event/great-outdoor-art-contest/ https://
 www.indianamuseum.org/event/great-outdoor-art-contest/\n\nCommunity Paint
  Together\n\n12 – 4 pm\n\nVillage Green\, Main & Jefferson\n\nFree and op
 en to the public\n\nThe Artist Associates of Brown County proudly present
 s the opportunity for everyone to take up a brush – young and old\, novic
 e and experienced. Families are welcome. The canvas will await those who 
 want to make their mark on this year’s masterpiece. A creation like no ot
 her\, the project aims to encourage the imaginative spirit and hidden tal
 ent within all of us.\n\nGuild Speaker Series\n\nRick Kelley\n\nBrown Cou
 nty Art History/Q&A\n\n1 – 2:30 pm\n\nBrown County Inn\n\nFree and open t
 o the public\n\nAs part of the 2026 Art Colony Weekend and in conjunction
  with the Art Colony Auction Preview\, join us for a fascinating journey 
 into the history of one of America's most celebrated art colonies.\n\nBro
 wn County historian and resident Rick Kelley will share his deep knowledg
 e of the Brown County Art Colony and the remarkable artists who came to t
 hese hills seeking inspiration\, community\, and a place to call home. Th
 rough engaging stories\, personal insights\, and historical anecdotes\, R
 ick brings the past to life\, revealing the people\, places\, and events 
 that shaped Brown County's rich artistic legacy. Rick will invite audienc
 e members to ask questions and share in the conversation.\n\nThe auction 
 is also available for preview\, 10am-1pm\n\n\nBrown County Art Gallery\n\
 nOpen 10am-5pm\n\nOne Artist Drive\, Nashville IN 47448\n\nEnjoy the exhi
 bition\, Theodore Clement Steele: Indiana's Master Impressionist from Mun
 ich to Brown County and at 2:00pm view the live play\, "Selma and the Pai
 nter" featuring Broadway actress Jill Tasker as TC Steele's wife Selma St
 eele. It is a tale of Selma's life in Brown County with T.C. and the hist
 ory of the House of the Singing Winds. Free - Limited Seating\n\nSunday /
  September 13\n\nBrown County Art Colony Auction\n\n11 – 1 pm Art auction
  preview\n\n1 – 4:30pm Art auction\n\nBrown County Inn\n\nFree and open t
 o the public\n\nLooking for that special piece to finish an arrangement o
 r round out your collection? Art auctions remind us that the value of art
  is not just in its price\, but in the stories\, history\, and emotions i
 t embodies. Join us for a dynamic afternoon and watch buyers compete for 
 pieces. The works of Midwest Art Colony artists will be featured along wi
 th award-winning artists of today. Their endurability remains\, regardles
 s of the era in which they were painted.\n\n-----------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBrown C
 ounty Art Guild – A not for profit organization located in the heart of d
 owntown Nashville\, Indiana. On display throughout its galleries is a pri
 zed collection of historic paintings as well as current works for sale fr
 om regional award-winning member artists. The Guild also offers member ar
 tist demonstrations\, workshops\, special exhibits and many other events 
 during the year. Gallery hours: March – December\, Monday – Saturday\, 11
  – 5 and Sunday\, 12 – 4 or by appointment.
CATEGORIES:Free,Nashville,Visual-Arts
