SUMMARY: Mulholland Drive w/Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:A complex tale of suspense set in sunshine-drenched Los Angel
 es\, the film follows a dark-haired amnesiac car crash victim and a blond
 e stranger who become new friends and investigatory partners as they atte
 mpt to solve the mystery of the dark-haired woman's true identity. In tru
 e Lynchian fashion\, this journey is an uneasy blend of innocence and cor
 ruption\, love and loneliness\, beauty and depravity. [147 min\; drama\; 
 English]\n\nThe Cinema is pleased to welcome noted David Lynch scholar Dr
 . Justus Nieland\, who will introduce the film and take part in a post-fi
 lm conversation with Dr. Ed Dallis-Comentale\, Assistant Vice President f
 or Arts and Humanities and Professor of English.\n\nNieland is Professor 
 of English and Film Studies and Chairperson of the Department of English 
 at Michigan State University. He is a scholar of modernism and a film and
  media historian and his book on Mulholland Drive will be published by th
 e BFI Film Classics Series this year. He is the author of David Lynch (Un
 iversity of Illinois Press\, 2012) and co-author of Film Noir: Hard-Boile
 d Modernity and the Cultures of Globalization\, among many other publicat
 ions.
CATEGORIES:
