SUMMARY: One Person\, No Vote: A lecture and Q&A with Carol Anderson
DESCRIPTION:One Person\, No Vote: How Voter Suppression is Destroying Our
  Democracy\, a lecture and Q&A with Carol Anderson\n\nCarol Anderson is t
 he Robert W. Woodruff Professor of African American Studies at Emory Univ
 ersity. She is the author of several bestselling books including: The Sec
 ond: Race and Guns in a Fatally Unequal America (2020)\; One Person\, No 
 Vote: How Voter Suppression Is Destroying Our Democracy (2018)\, which wa
 s long-listed for the National Book Award in Non-Fiction\; and the critic
 ally-acclaimed White Rage: The Unspoken Truth of our Racial Divide (2016)
 \, which won the 2016 National Book Critics Circle Award for Criticism an
 d was also a New York Times Bestseller\, a New York Times Editor’s Pick\,
  and listed on the Zora List of 100 Best Books by Black Woman Authors sin
 ce 1850. Professor Anderson is also the author of Eyes Off the Prize: The
  United Nations and the African-American Struggle for Human Rights\, 1944
 -1955 (Cambridge University Press)\, which was awarded both the Gustavus 
 Myers and Myrna Bernath Book Awards. Her book Bourgeois Radicals: The NAA
 CP and the Struggle for Colonial Liberation\,1941-1960 was published by C
 ambridge in 2014.\n\nShe is a member of the American Academy of Arts and 
 Sciences and the American Philosophical Society\, and a recipient of The 
 Ella Baker Lifetime Achievement Award from The Hurston/Wright Foundation.
 \n\nHer ground-breaking research has\, additionally\, been supported by f
 ellowships from the American Council of Learned Societies\, the Ford Foun
 dation\, National Humanities Center\, Harvard University\, and the Gilder
  Lehrman Institute of American History.\n\nThe College Arts + Humanities 
 Institute is pleased to present this event with support from the Ruth N. 
 Halls Humanities Fund and the College of Arts & Sciences at Indiana Unive
 rsity Bloomington.\n\nCART captioning and ASL interpretation will be prov
 ided for the event. There will be a Q&A after the event. Tickets limited 
 to 4 per person. Groups may contact cahi@iu.edu mailto:cahi@iu.edu to req
 uest a larger order.
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Free
