SUMMARY: Bloomington Boogies: the Bloomington Blues & Boogie Woogie Piano
  Festival
DESCRIPTION:On October 10 through 12\, 2026\, enjoy acclaimed artists at 
 Bloomington Boogies: The Bloomington Blues & Boogie Woogie Piano Festival
 . Featuring musicians who play boogie-woogie\, blues\, and related styles
  in free and ticketed performances\, Bloomington Boogies strives to intro
 duce young people to artists and various non-classical styles through pub
 lic concerts and free educational activities\, including school performan
 ces\, workshops\, and master classes.\n\nThe festival begins with free pe
 rformances throughout the day on Saturday\, Oct. 10th:\n\n• 11 a.m.\, Mon
 roe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th St.\, Bloomington - WFHB's "Saturd
 ay's Child" will feature pianists Yoshi "Z2"Tsuji and Rob Rio\n\n• 2 p.m.
 \, also at the History Center - multi-instrumentalist Deanna Bogart prese
 nts performance/workshop "Inside the Groove: Blues\, Boogie-Woogie & Impr
 ovisation." Youth and aspiring pianists are invited\; pre-registration re
 quired\, beginning Sept. 1 at the festival website Education page - bloom
 ingtonboogies.com/education\, https://bloomingtonboogies.com/education\, 
 limited to 75 people.\n\n• 5 p.m.\, John Waldron Arts Center\, 122 S. Wal
 nut St.\, Bloomington - pianist Dr. Keith McCutchen will present "A Tribu
 te to Three Entities: Blues\, Gospel\, and Jazz Piano”\; pre-registration
  required\, beginning Sept. 1 at the festival website Education page\, li
 mited to 60 people.\n\n• 8 p.m.\, Cardinal Spirits\, 922 S. Morton St.\, 
 Bloomington - accordionist Bruce "Sunpie" Barnes\, guitarist Matt Hampsey
 \, and special guest pianist Silvan Zingg.\n\nOn Sunday\, Oct. 11\, the B
 loomington Boogies 2026 Festival Concert takes place at the Buskirk-Chuml
 ey Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Ave.\, beginning at 3 p.m. Tickets are requi
 red\, and may be purchased in advance at the Buskirk-Chumley Theater Box 
 Office\, 114 E. Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington\, IN\, by phone at 812-323-30
 20\, or at http://buskirkchumley.org. General admission in advance for ad
 ults is $34\; $24 for under age 12\, plus handling fees. Food and beverag
 es will be available.\n\nArtists performing at festival events are coming
  from far and wide:\n\n• Rob Rio - Boogie-woogie/blues piano from Los Ang
 eles\n\n• Jason Marsalis - Jazz/blues vibraphone/drums from New Orleans\n
 \n• Deanna Bogart - Blues/boogie-woogie piano/sax from Palm Desert\, CA\n
 \n• "Sunpie" Barnes & Matt Hampsey - Zydeco/blues accordion and guitar fr
 om New Orleans\n\n• Dr. Keith McCutchen - Jazz/blues piano from Kentucky\
 n\n• Yoshi "Z2" Tsuji - Jazz/blues/New Orleans piano\, originally from Ja
 pan\, based in New Orleans\n\n• Special Guest Silvan Zingg - Boogie-woogi
 e/blues/jazz piano\, founder of the International Boogie Woogie Festival\
 , Lugano\, Switzerland\n\n• Craig Brenner - Blues/boogie-woogie piano\, f
 ounder of Bloomington Boogies\n\n• Rhythm Section: Gordon Bonham/guitar\,
  Joe Donnelly/sax\, Ron Kadish/bass\, and Dan Hostetler/drums\n\n• Lineup
  subject to change\n\nMore free events continue Monday\, Oct. 12th:\n\n• 
 Jason Marsalis will present a free workshop focusing on how one can take 
 music from the 20th century and bring it into the 21st\, and the importan
 ce of fundamentals for vibes and drums\, time and location to be announce
 d\; registration opens Sept. 1 at the festival Education page.\n\n• Zoe I
 mani Willingham will present a free workshop on jazz violin: “Jazz Improv
 isation 101 for String Players" at 4:30 p.m. at Fairview Elementary Schoo
 l\; registration opens Sept. 1 at the festival Education page.\n\n• Tri-N
 orth and Jackson Creek Middle Schools and Fairview and Templeton Elementa
 ry Schools will all enjoy free concerts by guest artists\; school concert
 s are for students\, faculty\, staff\, and invited guests.\n\nMajor Festi
 val Sponsors include In Memory of Tim DeBruicker\, Ann Schertz Photograph
 y\, Mark Wiedenmayer\, Jonathan Dyson\, Tom Noonan\, City of Bloomington 
 Arts Commission\, and Anonymous.\n\nFestival Underwriters include Bob Kis
 sel's Foundation\, Linda Handelsman\, and Mother Bear's Pizza.\n\nAdditio
 nal Supporters include Bloomingfoods Co-op Market\, Katie Anderson\, Bob 
 Arnove\, Tom Barwise\, Michele Brentano\, Bridges Musical Arts Youth Orga
 nization\, Cardinal Spirits\, Deep Roots Landscape Design\, Cheryl Franks
 \, Ken Grooms & Zain Mackey\, Monroe County History Center\, Open Stages 
 Grant from Constellation Stage & Screen & The City of Bloomington\, Val H
 aughton & Frank Motley\, Dan & Wendy Hogg\, Wayne Jackson\, Dan & Maggie 
 Kirwan\, Richard and René Malone\, Ed Marshall\, Jane Matranga\, Tanya Mi
 tchell-Yeager\, Albert Misan\, MPI Solar LLC\, Dan Ostas & Bet Savich\, K
 athy & Mike Romy\, Fred & Jennifer Schultz\, Larry Stahl\, Story Insights
 \, Templeton PTO\, and others listed at the festival website.\n\nMedia Sp
 onsors include WFHB\, Bloom Magazine\, and WFYI.\n\nFor information\, vis
 it bloomingtonboogies.com/ https://bloomingtonboogies.com/ or contact Cra
 ig Brenner\, tel. 812-929-1784\, email craigbrennerboogies@gmail.com mail
 to:craigbrennerboogies@gmail.com .
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Music,Festival,Piano
